Prompts vendored for the BEAM benchmark harness.

1. prompts/listing-20.txt, listing-21.txt, listing-44.txt
   Listings 20, 21 and 44 from:
   Beyond a Million Tokens: Benchmarking and Enhancing Long-Term Memory in LLMs
   https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.27246 (version 2)
   Copyright the paper's authors. Paper material is reproduced under CC BY 4.0:
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   The prompts are verbatim UTF-8 text from the arXiv v2 TeX source archive. The v2 HTML
   contains empty figures for these three listings, so the TeX source is authoritative.

2. prompts/released/*.txt
   The runtime values of the corresponding strings in the authors' released code,
   https://github.com/mohammadtavakoli78/BEAM at commit
   b2da22eac88bb0874c64665f13457eb99835774a (src/prompts.py,
   src/evaluation/compute_metrics.py, src/answer_probing_questions/long_term_memory_methods.py).
   Copyright (c) 2025 Mohammad Tavakoli, MIT License.
   These are the strings the harness sends.

provenance.json records each file's source and SHA-256. `run.ts --verify-prompts` re-downloads
both sources and compares every file byte for byte. Only runtime placeholder substitution is
performed; see ../README.md.

Dataset licensing is separate: Mohammadta/BEAM is CC BY-SA 4.0.
The pastdotdev/benchmarks dataset parser was consulted as an MIT-licensed reference.
No ExaBase prompts are included or used.
